  "summary": "In 1947 six men led by Thor Heyerdahl sailed a balsa raft from Callao, Peru, on 28 April and after 101 days at sea ran aground on a reef at Raroia in the Tuamotu Archipelago. Heyerdahl wanted to test whether prehistoric South Americans could have reached Polynesia by drifting on ocean currents.",
